    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50324" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vējento</span></b> , ōnis,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a surname in the Fabrician</i> gens.; esp., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A contemporary of Cicero</i>, <i>a
				judge in Rome</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 4, 16, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 3,
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> A.
			Fabricius Vejento, <i>a courtier under Nero</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 14,
				50</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Juv. 3, 185</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 113 al.</span></i></div>
